# the plots and tables ARE the deliverables - the README links to them, so they
# have to be in the repo or every image is a broken link on github.
#
# these used to be ignored, which is why acf_summary/ never made it up while the
# older plot folders did. the old ones had been committed before the ignore rule
# was added, so git kept tracking them and the problem stayed invisible.
#
# same for data/*.csv. END_DATE in data_pipeline.py is pinned, so the CSVs are
# meant to be reproducible fixtures rather than throwaway downloads. anyone
# cloning this should be able to run eda.py without hitting Yahoo first.

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

